  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening Public Financial Management, Anti-Corruption and Accountability Institutions in Sierra Leone</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To support a more effective and accountable executive that raises, allocates and uses public resources transparently to drive inclusive and sustainable development. To do this, the project will deliver stronger public expenditure management, revenue, oversight and anti-corruption institutions resulting in increases in revenue (from 13.8% of GDP in 2018 to 15% of GDP in 2023), increasingly effective action on corruption (increasing investigation and prosecution of anti-corruption cases), and improved public financial management, transparency and accountability.</narrative>
  </description>
